    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1033">

                <pb facs="1189" n="1077" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1077"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.628/133: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Neville</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-30T17:00:00-04:00">August 30, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>132. Your despatch 1425, August 9, third paragraph.<anchor n="65"
                        xml:id="d1033-f1"/></p>
                <pb facs="1190" n="1078" xml:id="pg1078"/>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>You may inform the Foreign Office that this Government is prepared to
                        present to the Japanese Government specific proposals.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Should the reply of the Foreign Office to your inquiry be in the
                        affirmative, you may inform the Foreign Office that arrangements have been
                        made for an expert of the Bureau of Fisheries to proceed immediately to
                        Tokyo.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>For various reasons no draft convention has been prepared. However, Bower
                        will be fully instructed in regard to inducements to be held out in the
                        various contingencies which might be expected to arise in the course of the
                        negotiations.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>We concur in the thought expressed in the last sentence of paragraph under
                        reference.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1033-f1" n="65" xml:id="d1033-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the third paragraph suggested postponement of conversations “pending
                    the arrival of Mr. Bower” with “formal proposals, presumably in the form of a
                    draft convention.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
